('GRE_3','GRE_3_5092','chagrin','ʃə''ɡrɪn','ʃə''grɪn','[n] 失望， 懊恼','To the chagrin of their parents, neither Phil nor Pam went to church anymore.  令父母失望的是，菲尔和帕姆都再也不去教堂了。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5093','predator','''prɛdətɚ','''predətər','[n] 食肉动物','With no natural predators on the island, the herd increased rapidly.  由于岛上没有天然食肉动物，牧群的数量迅速增加。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5094','forfeit','''fɔrfət','''fɔːrfət','[v] 丧失，被罚没收; [n] 丧失的东西','By being absent from the trial, he forfeited the right to appeal.  因缺席审判，他丧失了上诉权。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5095','bamboozle','bæm''buzl','bæm''buːzl','[v] 欺骗， 隐瞒','He bamboozled Mercer into defeat.  他蒙骗默瑟并击败了他。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5096','jaundice','''dʒɔndɪs','''dʒɔːndɪs','[n] 偏见； 黄疸','Leptospirosis causes severe jaundice, kidney failure and bleeding in the lungs.  钩端螺旋体导致严重的黄疸、肾衰竭和肺出血。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5097','straiten','''streitən','''str3ɪtən','[v] 使为难； 使变窄',''),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5098','euphemism','''jufəmɪzəm','''juːfəmɪzəm','[n] 婉言， 委婉的说法','‘Pass away’ is a euphemism for ‘die’.  “去世”是“死”的委婉语。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5099','burning','''bɝnɪŋ','''bɜːrnɪŋ','[adj] 燃烧的； 强烈的','She was rescued from a burning building.  她被人从着火的大楼里救了出来。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5100','groan','ɡron','groun','[v] 呻吟，叹息; [n] 呻吟， 叹息','The kids all groaned when I switched off the TV.  我关掉电视时，孩子们都发出不满的抱怨声。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5101','oleaginous',',olɪ''ædʒɪnəs','ˌouli''ædʒɪnəs','[adj] 油腻的； 圆滑的， 满口恭维的',''),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5102','plunder','''plʌndɚ','''plʌndər','[v] 抢劫， 掠夺','The rich provinces of Asia Minor were plundered by the invaders.  小亚细亚的富饶地区遭到侵略者的劫掠。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5103','distaste','dɪs''test','dɪs''teɪst','[v] 厌恶; [n] 厌恶， 不喜欢','She looked at his shabby clothes with distaste.  她厌恶地看着他褴褛的衣衫。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5104','expatiate','','ɪk''speɪʃieɪt','[v] 细说， 详述','I''m in such a drive that I can''t expatiate.  我的时间实在紧迫，不能详述。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5105','verbosity','','vɜːr''bɑːsəti','[n] 冗长','As expressions get more complicated the need to reduce the verbosity of type specification gets more compelling.  当表达式变得更加复杂，减轻类型说明的冗长的要求变得更加迫切。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5106','determinant','dɪ''tɝmɪnənt','dɪ''tɜːrmɪnənt','[adj] 决定性的; [n] 决定因素','I used this to remember how to calculate the determinant of a matrix.  我就用过这个方法来记住怎么算矩阵中的决定因素。'),
('GRE_3','GRE_3_5107','pelt','pɛlt','pelt','[v] 扔; [n] 毛皮','Some of the younger men began to pelt one another with snowballs.  一些年纪稍轻的人开始相互扔雪球。'),
